    "result_text": "The full suite is genuinely just the one acceptance test (the other two files are support classes: `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture`). Everything passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now also includes `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, with the previously-logged fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`) retained.\n\n**Change** in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Moved the `OwnerDto` mapping to *before* the audit call and sourced both membership values from it, so the logged values are exactly the derived ones a client reads back on `GET /owners/{id}`:\n  ```java\n  this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n  OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n      ownerDto.getMembershipLevel(), ownerDto.getMembershipNumber());\n  ```\n- Removed the now-unused `MembershipLevel` import (the level came from `MembershipLevel.forOwner(owner)`, which the mapper already applies to the DTO).\n\nReusing the DTO avoids duplicating the `membershipNumber` formatting logic (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) that lives in the mapper, keeping the audit value consistent with the API response by construction.\n\n**Result:** `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. Sample audit line emitted:\n```\nAUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-07 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```",
